# Template for .env — copy, don't rename:  cp .env.example .env
#
# .env holds real passwords and is gitignored, so this file is the only
# record in the repo of what a working install needs. Every value below is
# a placeholder: replace the <angle brackets> with your own.
#
# You do NOT need all of these. Which ones matter depends on what you run
# (see "Setup" in README.md):
#
#   reading/writing the database  -> DATABASE_URL
#   ingesting runs and segments   -> + SC_DATABASE_URL, POSITIONS_DATABASE_URL
#   applying the trap filter      -> + NABPY_PATH (only if nabPy is not
#                                     already importable in your env)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED: CalibrationNet itself — the `calibrationnet` schema inside the
# shared nab_db. Keep the search_path option; it is what keeps this
# project's tables separate from the rest of nab_db.

# Off-cluster, through an SSH tunnel you open first:
#   ssh -L 5432:<db-host>:5432 <user>@login-phoenix.pace.gatech.edu
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@localhost:5432/nab_db?options=-csearch_path%3Dcalibrationnet

# ON the cluster, reach the host directly — no tunnel, and much faster for
# bulk ingest. Use this line instead of the one above:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@<db-host>:5432/nab_db?options=-csearch_path%3Dcalibrationnet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed only by scripts/ingest_run.py (run metadata and segments).
# Both live at SNS and are reached through the tunnel that
# scripts/with_sc_tunnel.sh opens; the port must match SC_LOCAL_PORT there.

# Slow controls (read-only): run times, detector and beamline settings.
SC_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@127.0.0.1:15432/Nab_SlowControl

# Test archive (read-only): source-frame position readback (what run
# segments are derived from) and, for runs after 2026-07-21, the run
# settings that moved out of the instrument tables (biases, HV, ExB,
# temperatures). Same server, different database.
# Optional — if unset, it is derived from SC_DATABASE_URL by swapping in
# the `Test` database, which is usually what you want.
# POSITIONS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@127.0.0.1:15432/Test

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed only where the trap filter is applied (scripts/apply_trap_filter.py),
# and only if `python -c "import nabPy"` does NOT already work in that
# environment. Set it to the directory that CONTAINS the nabPy package —
# in a pyNab checkout that is its src/ directory:
#
#   NABPY_PATH=<path to your pyNab checkout>/src
#
# If nabPy is installed (e.g. by scripts/setup_env.sh, which pip-installs
# it), leave this unset.
# NABPY_PATH=
